WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.010
Kraken Island on the Adonia Sea?

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.680
I don't know it.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.350
Well, if you want to go to the port town,

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.840
it's fastest if you go over that mountain.

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:34.360
<i>That's how it always starts...</i>
<i>under the azure sky</i>

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:41.270
<i>After making a vow,</i>
<i>I now set off</i>

00:00:54.150 --> 00:01:00.660
<i>Yeah, the desert glitters with a golden hue</i>
<i>(The wind is scorching)</i>

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:07.000
<i>I'm searching for a diamond flower</i>
<i>(I keep on wandering)</i>

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:13.330
<i>Now, for the first time in my life,</i>

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:19.670
<i>I live for someone else</i>

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:26.180
<i>There's something</i>
<i>I wanna protect</i>

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:32.190
<i>I'll never,</i>
<i>ever lose it again</i>

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:35.690
<i>Resound,</i>
<i>my heartbeat!</i>

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:45.690
<i>A heartbeat smaller and fragile,</i>
<i>but tougher than anyone's.</i>

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:02.210
"Dozing Cat"

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:15.660
The fog has gotten quite thick...

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:17.330
Bro...

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:21.330
We have no choice but to wait
until the fog clears.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:26.010
No need to worry.
We'll catch up right away.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:28.010
Where are Glin and
the rest of the sweepers?

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:31.340
They're taking a different route
and are headed for the port.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:35.010
They said they're gonna get
the weapons and munitions.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.350
Are you really going with them?

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:40.580
I'll think about it
after I get a hold of Train.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:46.030
Wh- What is that?

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:48.090
I wonder if it's thunder?

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.360
It's the rumbling of the mountain.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:56.040
It's been like this for ages.
On foggy nights, you can hear it.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.710
The locals say that demons are fighting.

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:02.310
D- Demons?

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:06.370
It'd be wise if you stay indoors.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.780
What's that sound?

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.030
Saya!

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:48.680
Saya...

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:01.760
We're alike, aren't we?

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:05.400
Saya!

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.980
Oops! I'm sorry! My hand just lashed out,

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:18.010
but, you suddenly jumped up like that...

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:31.290
Hm? Aren't you going
to drink the herbal tea?

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:38.000
Your body must be cold
from the night mist.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.130
That will warm you up
and help you to sleep.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:47.680
I was shocked when I found you
collapsed in front of the house.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.740
I had such a hard time
bringing you to this bed.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:59.360
Oh, but I'm fine because working
in the mountains has made me strong.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:00.720
See?

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:06.970
Please don't stare at me like that.

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:09.330
Oh, yeah...

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.640
My name is Saki.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:13.970
Saki?

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:16.640
Yes. What's your name?

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:19.310
Train Heartnet.

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:21.310
Train-<i>kun</i>?

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:24.650
What a nice name, it sounds
like a traveler's name!

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.380
Are you traveling alone?

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.990
Well, traveling alone is fine,

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:36.660
but it was reckless
to walk in the fog like that.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:39.660
I wanted to reach the port by this morning.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:44.670
Life isn't meant to be rushed, you know.

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.670
It seems that you're exhausted, too,

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:50.010
so drink that and get some more sleep.

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:52.340
What is this?

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:54.400
Want to know?

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:00.050
No... never mind.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:06.790
It's bitter! No, awful!

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:09.960
Good medicine tastes bitter.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.830
But you'll be able to sleep well.

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:45.330
What's wrong, Train-<i>kun</i>?
You look so serious.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:48.000
I came all the way just to see you.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.470
Hurry over here.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.070
Saya!

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:03.070
Oww!

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:21.000
Oh, you're up!

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:37.650
This place is amazing!

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:41.650
It looks like some impregnable castle.

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:43.320
We all built it together.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:46.120
"We"? There are others?

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:48.660
Well, sorta...

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:50.000
I see...

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:51.290
Watch out!

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.610
Wow!

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:02.670
Look, you...

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:07.280
Cripes! Is this some ninja residence!?

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:09.840
Or are you trying to kill me?

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:12.620
Sorry, sorry!

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:16.290
A woman living alone can't be too careful.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:17.380
Hm?

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:35.210
Ahh! Milk's even better
when you drink it in the morning!

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:41.980
Hey, you're staring at me again.

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:44.650
Or perhaps, it's love at first sight?

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:47.680
N- No way!

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:57.320
So you like milk?

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:00.270
It's my favorite!

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:03.270
I can drink bucketfuls.

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:06.940
How do you get milk
so deep in the mountains?

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:09.240
Do you go down the mountain to buy stuff?

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:14.280
When we came here,
we all brought cows, chickens...

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:18.280
Anyway, we brought everything
we needed for everyday life...

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:20.950
so that we needn't ever go back down.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:22.960
It sounds just like an ark.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:26.630
Just what were you escaping from?

00:09:26.630 --> 00:09:30.630
Well... there are
all kinds of things in life.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:34.730
Hey, shall I show you around our house?

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:50.320
This is the library.

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:52.650
We wanted to keep
a record of our homeland,

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:55.420
so together we brought them here
although it was heavy.

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:00.020
A record of their homeland?

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:07.000
And this is the food storehouse...

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:10.300
though it's just a fruit-bearing tree
that we have in here...

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.370
Want to try one?

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.270
Oh, looks like it was overripe!

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:24.940
Why you!

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:31.020
I'll wash your clothes, okay?

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:33.360
Yeah.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:37.130
The weather's nice today,
so I guess I'll hang them out in the sun.

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:44.770
What a mess tha...

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:23.010
<i>How far shall we go</i>

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:32.680
<i>Looking up in the sky</i>

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:42.360
<i>A baby's first cry</i>

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:52.040
<i>The beating of an insect's wings</i>

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:56.710
<i>Lightly, ligh...</i>

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:59.180
Oh, you heard me singing?

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:02.650
Where'd you learn that song?

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:07.320
Hmm... I've been singing it
ever since I can remember.

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:09.990
So even if you asked me,
I can't really say.

00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:12.650
What about this song?

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:24.340
Yeah, it's good.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:26.000
Aren't you going to eat?

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:28.340
You look so serious.

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:30.680
Are you worried about something?

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:32.640
You should be more relaxed!

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:38.020
Aren't you the one
who's worried about something?

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:39.020
Like what?

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:40.690
Don't play dumb.

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:44.020
This castle-like house.
Books from a faraway country.

00:12:44.020 --> 00:12:46.360
Weapons I've never seen before...

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:49.690
And... you keep talking about others,

00:12:49.690 --> 00:12:51.600
but there's no one around!

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:59.700
To tell you the truth, we have
the power to foresee the future...

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:03.040
We were chased out of our homeland
by people who hated our power...

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:04.980
so we came here...

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:06.810
That's a crazy story...

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:12.650
We came here after being chased out,

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:17.280
And we've been protecting
something very precious for a long time.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:26.330
Something very precious, which we
brought with us from our homeland.

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:27.670
Some treasure?

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:29.000
No...

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:34.670
Our future, perhaps.

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:36.340
Future?

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:46.170
I understand. I won't ask again.

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:04.260
Here you are.
Herbal tea for after your meal.

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:17.880
Train-<i>kun</i>!

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:26.790
I fell asleep again...

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:42.430
It's still not dry.

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:16.070
Th- this is...

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:20.980
Yeah, it's had it.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:23.320
The garden's a mess.

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:25.650
It's not just the garden.

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:27.990
Who the hell did this?

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:31.320
They come around sometimes... wild dogs.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:32.660
Stop fooling with me!

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.990
It takes more than wild dogs to do all this!

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:38.660
It's a huge pack of wild dogs!

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:42.000
From ones that look scary like this
to ones that are unexpectedly cute...

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.340
About 30,000 of them run around...

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:48.330
Grrr, grrr, grrr!

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:59.020
Why don't you just tell me the truth?

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:01.710
Who are you fighting?

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:08.630
There are no others, are there?

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:09.960
I'll help you and...

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:12.300
Leave us alone!

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:14.630
How can I? After seeing this!?

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:17.970
Oh be quiet! This has nothing
to do with you, Train-<i>kun</i>!

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:20.640
Nothing to do...

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:22.970
You sure you really don't need help!?

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:27.310
No! Stop butting in and hurry up
and get off this mountain!

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:30.320
Oh yeah? Fine then!

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:32.750
I'll do just that once my clothes are dry!

00:16:59.340 --> 00:17:03.650
Hey, are you really going
to be all right by yourself?

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:11.010
I'll help you.

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:17.060
I don't want anyone to die anymore.

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:23.200
Drink your herbal tea while it's hot.

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:05.640
There's a lot of you this time!

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:29.730
You fool... there're too many
for you to handle all by yourself.

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:02.630
Game over.

00:19:03.940 --> 00:19:08.000
Dolls are usually manipulated by humans.

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:12.280
You lend a hand to evil?

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:14.950
Evil? You mean Saki?

00:19:14.950 --> 00:19:18.620
I'm talking about the "<i>midorigo"</i>
that she's protecting!
(<i>"midorigo" = a baby.</i>)

00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:19.950
<i>Midorigo</i>?

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:23.290
Once it's grown and
is released to the fields,

00:19:23.290 --> 00:19:25.960
there will certainly be calamity!

00:19:25.960 --> 00:19:29.630
I beg of you, traveler!
Take my place and do the deed!

00:19:29.630 --> 00:19:33.860
Destroy the seed of evil with your hands!
With that weapon!!

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:43.810
We were musketeers serving a king
who ruled in a faraway land,

00:19:43.810 --> 00:19:44.980
which you do not know.

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:47.310
Musketeers?

00:19:47.310 --> 00:19:52.650
One day, the queen bore
a darling crown prince.

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:56.820
But at that time, our gods
passed down this judgment...

00:19:57.990 --> 00:20:01.990
"The crown prince was born under
a tainted star that will bring disaster.

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:04.620
"Throw him into the darkness right away."

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:10.670
My comrades and I took
the prince and escaped.

00:20:10.670 --> 00:20:16.340
After all, how could we destroy
the future of a newborn babe?

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:20.570
Even if this babe did
bring calamity in the future...

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:25.020
He's heavy.

00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:27.350
That's how heavy the future is.

00:20:27.350 --> 00:20:31.520
He bears the weight
of happiness and sadness.

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:37.030
But in order to protect his future,

00:20:37.030 --> 00:20:39.930
the future of all my comrades
were sacrificed.

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:54.070
Well, I'm sure your comrades
have no regrets.

00:20:57.050 --> 00:21:00.380
Because they were able to
make a run of it with you until death.

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:05.390
Aren't comrades like that?

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:14.520
Train-<i>kun</i>... where are your comrades?

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:20.240
They're all waiting for you.

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:22.940
Saya!

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:29.010
Owwee!

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:30.350
What the hell are you doing!?

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:34.020
Shut up! Causing us so much worry!

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:35.020
Cripes!

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:38.360
You need another ten years before
you can try to steal a march on me!

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:40.360
You're like the bug flying
into the flame on a summer night.

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:42.360
Bro!

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:45.160
What do you think you can do alone?

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:51.700
Well, shall we go?

00:21:51.700 --> 00:21:56.040
Hah! Who needs help from you guys!?

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:57.040
Bro!

00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:59.380
Hey Train! Not again!

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:00.650
Hurry up and follow him!

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:02.200
Oh, yeah!

00:22:05.980 --> 00:22:07.350
Out of gas...

00:22:14.320 --> 00:22:21.330
<i>Since your new black boots</i>
<i>caused a blister,</i>

00:22:21.330 --> 00:22:28.340
<i>you rest your right foot</i>

00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:38.340
<i>We'll keep walking along</i>
<i>with our own rhythm, without rushing</i>

00:22:41.850 --> 00:22:51.850
<i>Don't say anything</i>
<i>because we'll soon understand each other</i>

00:22:56.400 --> 00:23:06.400
<i>I'm just holding you now to keep you warm</i>

00:23:10.650 --> 00:23:20.640
<i>I'm completely wrapped around you, so...</i>

00:23:21.060 --> 00:23:31.050
<i>Quietly the powder-like snow</i>
<i>is building up...</i>

00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:41.010
"Next Episode"

00:23:41.010 --> 00:23:42.680
<i>Well, we've come all the way here...</i>

00:23:42.680 --> 00:23:44.680
<i>to the farthest port town.</i>

00:23:44.680 --> 00:23:47.680
<i>And across the sea is the island</i>
<i>of the Apostles of the Stars.</i>

00:23:47.680 --> 00:23:51.350
<i>Well, I guess I'll set my mind to it</i>
<i>and go for it.</i>

00:23:51.350 --> 00:23:56.020
<i>Actually, I'd like to leave</i>
<i>Eve and Train behind...</i>

00:23:56.020 --> 00:23:58.690
<i>But there's no way they'd listen...</i>

00:23:58.690 --> 00:24:01.960
<i>Geez... My life is</i>
<i>one worry after another...</i>

00:24:01.960 --> 00:24:02.430
<i>What? I've got gray hairs?</i>

00:24:02.430 --> 00:24:03.460
"Cat Sets Sail"
<i>What? I've got gray hairs?</i>

00:24:03.460 --> 00:24:05.000
<i>Where? Where'd you find them!?</i>
"Cat Sets Sail"

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:05.400
"Cat Sets Sail"
